{"name":"Beach Cabana","hex":"#a69081","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"},{"term":"cabana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cabin or hut for relaxing.","A shelter on a beach or at a swimming pool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"},{"title":"Cabana","blocks":[{"text":"A cabana is a type of shelter often found near beaches or pools. A cabana can be used to relax in the shade or change clothes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Cabana_%28structure%29.jpg/330px-Cabana_%28structure%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabana","wikidata":"Q3649129"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=